ameter \\(AP\\), this centre lies on\nthe line \\(AP\\).  Applying \\(\\mathcal S_A\\) and using (1) we obtain that the image is the\nmid‑point of the arc \\(EF\\) of the circle \\((BEF)\\).  Hence the centre \\(O\\) of\n\\((BEF)\\) also lies on the line \\(\\ell_A\\) defined in (2).  Consequently  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\;O\\in\\ell_A\\quad\\text{and}\\quad O A\\perp AB\\;}. \\tag{5}\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 8.  Tangency\n\nFrom (4) the line \\(\\ell\\) is parallel to \\(AP\\); from (2) the image of \\(AP\\) under\n\\(\\mathcal S_A\\) is \\(\\ell_A\\), which is perpendicular to \\(AB\\).  Because \\(\\mathcal\nS_A\\) is a similarity, it preserves oriented angles; therefore the angle between\n\\(\\ell\\) and \\(AB\\) equals the angle between \\(\\ell_A\\) and \\(AB\\), i.e. \\(90^{\\circ}\\).\nThus  \n\n\\[\n\\ell\\perp AB .\n\\tag{6}\n\\]\n\nFrom (5) the centre \\(O\\) of \\((BEF)\\) lies on the line through \\(A\\) perpendicular to\n\\(AB\\); hence \\(OB\\) is also perpendicular to \\(AB\\).  Combining (6) we obtain  \n\n\\[\n\\ell\\perp OB .\n\\]\n\nA line through a point of a circle that is perpendicular to the radius drawn to that\npoint is the **tangent** at the point.  Therefore \\(\\ell\\) is tangent to \\((BEF)\\) at\n\\(B\\).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 9.  Conclusion  \n\nThe line through the orthocentre \\(H\\) of \\(\\triangle PMN\\) that is parallel to \\(AP\\)\nis tangent to the circum‑circle of \\(\\triangle BEF\\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{The required tangency holds.}}\n\\]"
